# ML Pipeline for Social Media Engagement Prediction

## Overview
This project predicts social media engagement using machine learning techniques. The goal is to analyze social media post data, engineer useful features, and train classification models to predict engagement levels.

This was my first machine learning project and helped me understand the complete ML workflow from data preprocessing to model evaluation.

---

## Project Workflow

1. Data Collection and Loading
2. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
3. Data Cleaning and Preprocessing
4. Feature Engineering
5. Model Training
6. Model Evaluation
7. Model Comparison

---

## Dataset

The dataset contains information related to social media posts and engagement metrics.

Example features include:

- Impressions
- Likes
- Shares
- Comments
- Reach
- Clicks
- Engagement Rate

---

## Models Used

### 1. Logistic Regression
A linear classification algorithm used as the baseline model.

### 2. Decision Tree Classifier
A tree-based model capable of capturing non-linear relationships in data.

### 3. Random Forest Classifier
An ensemble learning model that combines multiple decision trees to improve prediction performance.

---

## Model Performance

| Model | Accuracy |
|-------|----------|
| Logistic Regression | 50.58% |
| Decision Tree | 94.29% |
| Random Forest | 95.92% |

The Random Forest Classifier achieved the highest accuracy and performed best on the dataset.

